# From "The Absolute" (Wave VIII - Union, CD4-8), Monroe's own term for
# completing the reincarnation cycle -- kept faithfully, per the user's
# explicit call 2025-10-10. Structurally the same as every other segment: it
# closes with the standard return-to-full-waking-consciousness count, one
# more visit like the rest of the wave, not a departure from that pattern.

@segment  the-absolute
@title    The Absolute
@levels   F27
@duration ~5m

say From your special place, relax. Take a deep breath.
pause 6
say Consider your current embodiment in the Earth-life system. Your beliefs. Your fears, your loves. Your sorrows, your joy, your pain.
pause 8
say Simply observe all of it, and let some distance open up. Notice: the one observing isn't actually any of these things.
pause 10
say Now consider your self-image -- the one you've worked so hard to build, to maintain, to show to everyone you meet. Your body. Your education. Your job. Your country.
pause 8
say Observe all of it the same way, with that same distance. Realize the one observing isn't any of it. They're constructs -- all of them. See this clearly now.
pause 10
say If you feel ready -- if you're a last-timer, as Bob Monroe put it -- you need not remain in the physical earth-life system. Let your consciousness move, slowly, from your special place into the other areas of the reception center.
pause 10
say A long hallway opens before you, doors on either side. Move toward it.
pause 8
say Ahead is a large box, with a heavy lid. Place the totality of your experience from Earth inside it -- your embodiments, your beliefs, your fears, your goals, your unresolved desires. Thank them for their service, and leave them there.
pause 12
say Close the lid, and move on down the hallway, past the doors.
pause 8
say At the very end, one final door.
pause 6
say When you're ready, open it, and step through.
pause 8
say Let go, and observe.
hold 60
say Give thanks for what you've experienced. It's time to return, to the Earth-life system.
pause 6
